  "purpose": "Find the exact root cause of Phase 12D's release-crash and the minimal safe rule for freeing a relocated KV layer's old backing, so that runtime relocation can be paired with real memory reclamation instead of a permanent leak.",
  "literal_verdict": "KV_BUFFER_RETIREMENT_VIABLE",
  "verdict_summary": "Root cause identified by source trace, not guesswork: the crash was never in ggml_backend_sched or in Vulkan's tensor metadata (both ruled out directly) -- it is llama_context::gf_res_prev, a cached llm_graph_result from the PREVIOUS decode call that llama_context transparently RE-EXECUTES unchanged whenever res->can_reuse(gparams) returns true (llama-context.cpp:1336), which happens on essentially every same-shape autoregressive step. That reuse path skips the cpy_v/get_v calls that would re-read the relocated layer's new backing, so it keeps executing stale views over backing that relocate_layer's cleanup has since freed. The fix (llama_invalidate_graph_cache(), 145 insertions/6 deletions, 5 files) forces a rebuild after any relocation; with it, IMMEDIATE retirement is safe -- no delay or generation-counting needed. 50/50 and 20/20 repeated cycles showed zero VRAM/RSS creep, and real memory reclamation was proven up to the ctx=200000/360M GTX-1650 pressure boundary (3107 -> 3237 -> 3105 MiB, promote then retire returns to baseline).",
  "verdict_source": "results/phase12/buffer-retirement/summary.json:decision_gate / decision_gate_meaning (literal source fields, not synthesized)",
  "productized": false,
  "product_pr": null,
  "product_commit": null,
  "productization_note": "Verified: `git grep` for llama_invalidate_graph_cache / retire_layer_backing against product main returns no hits. This remains research-only. This phase completed the technical proof that dynamic KV movement CAN be made memory-safe -- but Phase 12F/12G's findings are what determined it was not worth shipping (no measured performance win at tested scale).",
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
  "hardware": "NVIDIA GTX 1650 (4096 MiB VRAM), Vulkan backend",
  "models": [
    "SmolLM2-135M-Instruct",
    "SmolLM2-360M-Instruct"
  ],
